#42000
Where the Blackwood Weeps~
   The black, dripping trees of the Blackwood thin out here, and
something about the forest changes.  The mist grows thicker and colder,
and the trees ahead are of another kind altogether, pale and twisted,
their bark gathered into knots and hollows that look disturbingly like
faces.  A faint path, little more than a parting in the mist, leads
north between them.  The Blackwood lies to the west.
~
