#42004
In the Ghost-Light~
   The maddening darkness is giving way here to an eerie, ghostly light
that seems to come from nowhere and everywhere at once.  In it you can
see that the trees are more than trees: their bark has gathered into
faces, horribly sad faces, and their limbs reach out like arms begging
for a help that never comes.  The wind still swirls about you, sounding
like echoed cries for release.  By the new light you can see that the
figure ahead of you is a cloaked man, now either resting or perhaps
awaiting your arrival.  His careless air makes you wary.  The path
continues north and south.
~
