#42012
A Row of Open Graves~
   A long row of graves has been dug here, all open and all empty,
waiting.  Each has a headstone already set at its head, but the stones
are blank.  A cold draft rises out of the open earth, and the bottom of
every grave is lost in shadow.  The graveyard continues north and east,
and a tumbledown hut leans against an old yew tree to the west.
~
