#42026
The Hall of Two Faces~
   This long hall is divided down its length by a line of black and
white tiles.  To the west, on the white side, stands a door of pale
marble carved with the face of a young woman, her eyes closed as if in
sleep; it has no handle, no lock and no seam that you can find.  To the
east, on the black side, an open archway carved with the face of a
laughing young man leads into darkness.  The landing lies to the south.
~
